   "text": "9. Poor sleep\n\nLook at the clock on the chart. 3:17 in the morning, wide awake.\n\nNormally, your cortisol is at its lowest around midnight. That helps you fall asleep and stay asleep. With Cushing's, cortisol stays high at night, so sleep can be really hard.\n\nThat's one way",
   "url": "https://x.com/WisdomLifeHack/status/2119058654376669470"
